# Lesson 5, new exercise: Stayman over a 2NT opening, spade fit found.
title: Stayman over 2NT: a spade fit
id: L05-13
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.7
student: S
board: 25
dealer: N
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AKQ7   J82    K5     AKQ5
  E  J2     A9753  JT7    987
  S  9653   KT4    Q64    J62
  W  T84    Q6     A9832  T43

auction:
  N 2NT    = 21-22 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 3C*    = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
     key: Over 2NT, 3♣ is Stayman. You need only 4 points, because partner has 21-22.
     not Pass: 6 points opposite 21-22 makes 27-28: plenty for game.
     not 3NT: You have four spades. Ask with 3♣ first.
  W Pass
  N 3S     = Four spades, not four hearts
  E Pass
  S 4S*    = Game in spades
     key: You've found a 4-4 spade fit and enough points for game.
     not 3NT: You have an 8-card spade fit. Play in spades.
     not Pass: You have enough for game. Bid it.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2NT showed 21-22, so with your 6 you knew there was a game.
  Stayman works over 2NT exactly as over 1NT, one level higher. Partner had
  four spades, so you bid 4♠. North is declarer, because North bid spades
  first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E DJ  S D4  W D2  N DK
  2   N SA  E S2  S S3  W S4
      note: Draw trumps.
  3   N SK  E SJ  S S5  W S8
      note: Keep drawing trumps.
  4   N SQ  E H3  S S6  W ST
      note: Trumps are drawn.
  5   N CA  E C7  S C2  W C3
      note: Run the clubs, starting with the top honors.
  6   N CK  E C8  S C6  W C4
      note: Keep going.
  7   N CQ  E C9  S CJ  W CT
      note: The clubs have split 3-3 so far.
  8   N C5  E H5  S H4  W D3
      note: Nobody else has a club left, so the 5 wins.
  9   N HJ  E H7  S HK  W H6
      note: Lead toward dummy's ♥K: if West has the ace, the king wins.
  10  S DQ  W DA  N D5  E D7
      note: Lead the ♦Q to set up the ♦K.
  11  W D9  N S7  E DT  S D6
      note: Declarer ruffs.
  12  N H8  E H9  S HT  W HQ
      note: Exit with a heart.
  13  W D8  N H2  E HA  S S9
      note: 11 tricks: 4♠ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: draw trumps, then run the clubs. Once the other clubs are
  gone, the fourth one is a winner too.

  4♠ made 11 tricks. 3NT would also have made, with nine tricks, so the
  wrong choice would not have cost the game this time. But 4♠ scored more,
  and with a 4-4 major fit the suit contract is usually the better bet.
